#!/usr/sbin/nft -f

# Keep the admin board off the captive bridge.
#
# This include is loaded inside fw4's `inet` table (see 20-nds-enforce.nft and
# 30-backend-firewall.nft for the same shape), so it runs on `fw4 reload` and
# survives a nodogsplash restart.
#
# WHAT IS BEING BLOCKED. uhttpd.admin serves the owner-facing admin board on
# :8090 over plain HTTP with `ubus_prefix=/ubus`, i.e. the board's login form
# and rpcd's session endpoint share that one cleartext origin. The session is
# what stands in front of ACL group `tollgate`, which grants
# `file:["exec"]`, `system:["password_set"]` and `tollgate wallet_drain_cashu`:
# arbitrary command execution as root, a root password change, or the
# operator's money. The opt-in TLS listener is :8443 — the same board, so it
# is dropped too.
#
# WHO CAN REACH IT TODAY. Captive clients live on br-lan (the shipped
# nodogsplash `gatewayinterface`, written by setup_nodogsplash in
# 99-tollgate-setup), both before payment and after: 20-nds-enforce.nft only
# hooks `forward`, and fw4's lan-zone input policy accepts what is left, so
# reaching :8090 was a matter of connecting to the open SSID. The board is
# owner-facing and is not part of the customer journey, so the captive bridge
# does not get it.
#
# WHY BOTH LAYERS. Dropping the :8090/:8443 entries from nodogsplash's pre-auth
# allow list (assert_nodogsplash_allow_entries, same commit series) is the
# node-scoped fix, but that list is written by two scripts and repaired on
# install — this rule is the one that does not depend on the list being in the
# intended state, and the only one that also covers an *authenticated* guest,
# whose traffic 20-nds-enforce.nft accepts by mark.
#
# CAVEAT, same as 30-backend-firewall.nft:15-17 — this assumes the captive
# bridge is named br-lan, which is what the shipped nodogsplash configuration
# and every other TollGate firewall rule assume. An operator who renamed the
# bridge loses this rule and nothing else.
#
# OPERATOR NOTE — what changes for you: the board answers on the private
# network (br-private, which nodogsplash does not gate) and on loopback; it no
# longer answers a client on br-lan. If you run with the private network
# disabled and administer the router from a br-lan client, use the module CLI
# (`tollgate status`, `tollgate wallet balance`, ...) or LuCI on :8080 instead.
#
# Deliberately NOT dropped here: :2050/:2051 (the captive portal the guest is
# paying through), :2121 (handled by 30-backend-firewall.nft), and :8080 (LuCI,
# kept reachable pre-auth on purpose — see
# docs/architecture/uhttpd-redirect-https-ownership-decision.md).

chain admin_board_input_guard {
	type filter hook input priority -1; policy accept

	meta nfproto ipv4 iifname "br-lan" tcp dport { 8090, 8443 } counter drop
	meta nfproto ipv6 iifname "br-lan" tcp dport { 8090, 8443 } counter drop
}
